{"diagnosis": "NOP fetch traps with `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `FAIL 0xdead` instead of progressing. picosoc/picosoc.v:127 and picosoc/picosoc.v:130 show mem_ready/mem_rdata combinationally valid during mem_xfer, so fresh mem_rdata is expected. picorv32.v:384 selects mem_rdata_q when (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) and mem_rdata otherwise, using stale data on the transfer cycle and decoding garbage to trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -384,1 +384,1 @@
-	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
+	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata : mem_rdata_q;", "expected": "PASS tohost (not FAIL 0xdead) with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted"}

